# AI Model Indicate Walkthrough

The AI model name is now being passed to the frontend to ensure users know exactly what is generating the responses. 

## Changes Made
- **Backend Chunking**: 
  - Updated [backend/routers/brief.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/routers/brief.py) to yield a metadata chunk prior to the text stream chunks.
  - The metadata yields a structure `{"meta": {"model": "..."}}`.
- **Frontend Logic Integration**:
  - Expanded `api.stream` inside [frontend/lib/api.ts](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/lib/api.ts) with a new `onMeta` callback to specifically parse and manage these metadata JSON events.
  - Upgraded both [frontend/hooks/useChat.ts](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/hooks/useChat.ts) and [frontend/app/page.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/app/page.tsx) with logic to capture the `meta.model` property and append it to the chat message context.
- **UI Enhancements**:
  - [DailyBriefChat.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/chat/DailyBriefChat.tsx) was enhanced to conditionally render a `• ✨ [model_name]` tag directly to the right of the timestamp inside each assistant message container.

## How to Verify
Open the CraftCanvas dashboard layout and send a chat message via Command Center or right sidebar. As the stream resolves, you'll see a sparkles icon accompanied by the AI model being actively queried (such as `gemini-2.5-flash` or the selected [ollama](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/ai_service.py#261-283) model) next to the message timestamp.
